  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Education obligated $2.4B in contracts in FY2026 to date across 780 awards, with an average award size of $3.1M. Obligations fell 3.2% year over year. Year-to-year totals show FY21 at $2.7B, FY22 at $2.4B, FY23 at $2.4B, FY24 at $2.7B, FY25 at $2.5B, and FY26 at $2.4B. Spending concentrates in financial services and IT categories: Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation received $936M, and Computer Systems Design Services received $693M. Vendor concentration is notable: ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $372M and NELNET SERVICING LLC received $300M. The mix of categories and top vendors points to continuing emphasis on loan servicing, payment processing, research, and IT systems work. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Education's contract spending trended year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Education obligated $2.4B in FY2026 to date and obligations fell 3.2% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $2.7B in FY21, $2.4B in FY22, $2.4B in FY23, $2.7B in FY24, and $2.5B in FY25. The FY2026 total reported so far equals the FY22 and FY23 totals and remains a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors account for most Education spending?",
        "body": "Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation is the largest category at $936M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $693M and Other Computer Related Services at $166M. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC leads vendors with $372M, followed by NELNET SERVICING LLC at $300M and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $243M. The top categories and vendors reflect large allocations to credit intermediation, loan servicing, and IT systems work."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Education spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Education obligated $2.4B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 780 awards with an average award size of $3.1M, and obligations fell 3.2% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $2.7B in FY21, $2.4B in FY22, $2.4B in FY23, $2.7B in FY24, and $2.5B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Education buy?",
      "a": "Education buys services concentrated in financial and information technology categories. Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation received $936M, Computer Systems Design Services received $693M, and Other Computer Related Services received $166M, with additional spending across research, custom programming, consulting, and data processing categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Education's largest contractors?",
      "a": "ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC is the largest contractor at $372M, followed by NELNET SERVICING LLC at $300M and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $243M. Other top vendors include EDFINANCIAL SERVICES LLC at $201M, MISSOURI HIGHER EDUCATION LOAN AUTHORITY at $138M, and MAXIMUS FEDERAL SERVICES, INC. at $132M."
